      ⍝ regression (Roy Tobin, bug-apl@gnu.org, 2026-08-04 and 2026-08-07):
      ⍝ )COPY/)LOAD of a file that fails every format sniff right at
      ⍝ offset 0 (e.g. /dev/null: opens fine, but is truly zero bytes)
      ⍝ used to leave XML_Loading_Archive's tag_name/attributes/end_attr
      ⍝ members uninitialized -- next_tag() hits EOF before ever setting
      ⍝ them, but nothing checked that, so is_tag()/print_tag() went on
      ⍝ to read through the garbage pointer. Reproducibly a SEGFAULT
      ⍝ under valgrind (deterministic there: the uninitialized tag_name
      ⍝ reads back as exactly NULL) and allocator-layout-dependent
      ⍝ without it. Fixed by zero-initializing all three in the
      ⍝ constructor and guarding is_tag() against tag_name==0.
      ⍝
      ⍝ Separately: Sys.hh checked #if HAVE_MMAN_H but configure.ac only
      ⍝ ever defines HAVE_SYS_MMAN_H, so the real mmap()-based Sys::mmap()
      ⍝ had never been compiled into any build -- every build silently
      ⍝ used a read()-based fallback instead. With that typo fixed, the
      ⍝ real mmap() started being used, and mmap()ing 0 bytes is invalid
      ⍝ (POSIX: EINVAL) -- Archive.cc's XML_Loading_Archive constructor
      ⍝ treated *any* mmap() failure as WS_FULL, so a merely-empty file
      ⍝ was misdiagnosed as "workspace file could not be mapped" instead
      ⍝ of "wrong format" (caught by Roy again, 2026-08-07: incorrectly
      ⍝ accepted as "intentional" in an earlier version of this comment
      ⍝ -- it was not). Fixed by checking file_length==0 explicitly
      ⍝ before ever calling mmap(), matching the "diagnose as wrong
      ⍝ format" behavior of every other unrecognized-content file.
      ⍝
      ⍝ A related bug Roy found in the same report: even for a file that
      ⍝ *is* correctly diagnosed (e.g. /etc/hosts, "does not have the
      ⍝ format ..."), )COPY/)LOAD had no way to know the constructor had
      ⍝ already rejected the content, so execution fell through into
      ⍝ read_Workspace() anyway and produced a second, confusing error
      ⍝ ("Got tag ... when expecting tag Workspace ... DOMAIN ERROR").
      ⍝ Fixed by adding XML_Loading_Archive::is_valid_format() (false
      ⍝ once the constructor prints the format diagnostic) and checking
      ⍝ it in Workspace::copy_WS()/load_WS() right after the existing
      ⍝ is_open() check, returning immediately instead of proceeding.
      ⍝
      ⍝ The file-format diagnostic itself goes to CERR (not compared
      ⍝ here, like other CERR-only warnings elsewhere in this suite);
      ⍝ with both fixes, )COPY/)LOAD /dev/null no longer raise any APL
      ⍝ error at all (nothing left to WS_FULL or fall through on), so
      ⍝ neither needs ]EXPECT any more.
      ⍝
      )COPY /dev/null
      )SIC

      )LOAD /dev/null

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ same regression, but for a *non-empty* file that fails the format
      ⍝ check (i.e. the /etc/hosts case from Roy's report, reproduced
      ⍝ with a self-contained scratch file instead of a system path):
      ⍝ before the is_valid_format() fix, )COPY still printed the
      ⍝ correct diagnostic but then fell through into read_Workspace()
      ⍝ anyway, raising a second, confusing "Got tag ... when expecting
      ⍝ tag Workspace ... DOMAIN ERROR". )SI below (nothing suspended,
      ⍝ so no output at all) confirms neither that nor any other error
      ⍝ was raised.
      H←'w' ⎕FIO[3] '/tmp/COPY_test_garbage.xml'
      R←('not xml content, deliberately wrong format') ⎕FIO[7] H
      ⎕FIO[4] H
0
      )COPY /tmp/COPY_test_garbage.xml
      )SI
      R←⎕FIO[19] '/tmp/COPY_test_garbage.xml'

      ⍝ regression (David Alden, bug-apl@gnu.org, 2026-09-27): )PCOPY of a
      ⍝ )DUMPed (.apl) workspace behaved exactly like )COPY, silently
      ⍝ overwriting an already-existing variable/function of the same name
      ⍝ instead of protecting it, as documented ("Protective )COPY. Same as
      ⍝ )COPY above, but not overwriting existing defined functions and
      ⍝ variables"). Root cause: )COPY/)PCOPY of a )DUMPed file re-executes
      ⍝ its source lines through InputFile::COPY_filter, which only ever
      ⍝ checked object *names* against an explicit )COPY object list and
      ⍝ had no concept of protection at all -- and the filter was skipped
      ⍝ entirely whenever there was no explicit object list, exactly the
      ⍝ common "'')PCOPY wsname'' with no object names" case reported here.
      ⍝ The )SAVEd (.xml) )PCOPY path was already correct (Archive.cc's
      ⍝ read_Symbol() checks protection independently of any object list);
      ⍝ only the )DUMPed (.apl) path shared none of that logic. Fixed by
      ⍝ adding a protection flag to InputFile::COPY_filter, consulting
      ⍝ Workspace::lookup_existing_symbol() from both the function- and
      ⍝ variable-name branches of check_filter(), and running the filter
      ⍝ whenever protection is requested even without an explicit object
      ⍝ list.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )DROP PCOPY_tc
³

